2oo|n|To go up; to ascend. ; To rise or reach by an accumulation of particular sums or quantities; to come (to) in the aggregate or whole; -- with to or unto. ; To rise, reach, or extend in effect, substance, or influence; to be equivalent; to come practically (to); as, the testimony amounts to very little. ; The sum total of two or more sums or quantities; the aggregate; the whole quantity; a totality; as, the amount of 7 and 9 is 16; the amount of a bill; the amount of this year's revenue. ; The effect, substance, value, significance, or result; the sum; as, the amount of the testimony is this.	a:f0i,75,4;qw1,68,7;18aa,67,3;1yy6,66,3;i3a,57,6;22ft,56,7;1unl,55,6;ynt,52,5;bn5,49,8;167n,47,3~1593,39,10;1ru6,21,8;bn5,49,8;22ft,56,7;qw1,68,7;1vhw,28,7;i3a,57,6;1unl,55,6;1udo,37,5;1qmx,18,5	v:jc2,50,5~jc2,50,5	n:1q4p,37,8;qp1,26,8;19qd,19,1~qp1,26,8;1q4p,37,8;19qd,19,1
